D.2 The Skill of "Judgment of Judgment"

The Architect’s irreplaceable human skill — the one that cannot be delegated to AI — is knowing when to trust human intuition and when to trust AI calculation. As recent research on automation bias in agentic AI shows, humans in high‑stakes environments often prefer higher levels of agency than experts deem strictly necessary. The Architect must distinguish between:

· Wisdom: The human who hesitates because they notice something subtle that the AI's sensors haven't processed
· Fear: The human who hesitates because they are unfamiliar with the AI's reliable operational patterns

The decision topology is designed to accommodate the first and engineer around the second. No certification exam can test this judgment — it is evaluated only through analog deployment performance and board recommendation.

